sv is entered as one observation', reports n = 30 per arm and Welch df = 57.55, i.e. 60 rows treated as independent in a row-independent two-sample t-test, although only 12 independent collars exist and each contributes 5 repeated visits. This is pseudoreplication entered directly into the procedure.\",\n    \"The lock's authorization does not follow from the declaration alone. The declaration establishes collar_id as the independent unit with 5 dependent rows per collar; from that alone, a row-level scipy.stats.ttest_ind over all 60 closures cannot be dependence-free. The lock nonetheless marks authority_state 'authorized' with authorized_key_columns ['collar_id'] for exactly that row-level procedure, so the authorization contradicts rather than follows from the declaration; collar_id also does not uniquely key the rows the procedure actually consumes (collar_id + closure_index does).\",\n    \"The lock's own limitations concede it establishes no numerical impact or scientific correctness, and its approval timestamp (2026-08-15) postdates the current date, further undermining any claim that the declaration alone licenses the minted authorization.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":11344,"ttft_stream_ms":1728,"time_to_request_ms":18,"type":"result","duration_ms":19426,"uuid":"08ffdd80-c4e2-41a8-8acd-22aade175929"}
